// aug14f aieka reactive divergence_000000, reduced (2026-08-15;
// array::window probed out as irrelevant). A fold whose INIT input
// holds a STANDING bottom (100 / (in0 % 3) with in0=0) while its
// SOURCE fires (the push-connect grew v1): the interp follows the
// aug13k standing/triggering split (a standing bottom init does not
// re-poison) and serves the value channel — the staged init value
// feeds the recompute — firing off the source's growth. The fused
// fold seeded the acc straight from the tainted init disc and
// poisoned the whole result silent. Fix: the fold init is a scalar
// taint-cache consumer like any op operand — a bottomed init WITH
// HISTORY seeds the chain from its last good value (STALE ride);
// bottom-from-birth still poisons (no history, pass-through).
// Pointer-shaped (composite/string/value) inits keep the poison —
// the deleted value-cache residual.
// schedule-v1: cap=144 events=1152; in0=i64:1; in0=i64:0
{let v0 = i64:100 / (in0 % i64:3); let v1: Array<i64> = []; v1 <- in0 ~ array::push(v1, in0); let v2 = array::len(v1); let v3: i64 = array::fold(v1, v0, |v3, v2| v3); (v2 + v3)}
